INSERT INTO kingdom_verses (verse_id, strand, strand_label, card_title, card_md, anchor_refs, tier_required, last_reviewed_at)
VALUES ((SELECT v.id FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON c.id = v.chapter_id JOIN books b ON b.id = c.book_id JOIN editions e ON e.id = b.edition_id WHERE e.slug = 'canon' AND b.slug = 'revelation' AND c.chapter_number = 5 AND v.verse_number = 9), 'gathering', 'The gathering', 'Redeemed Out of Every Nation', $card$*And they sung a new song, saying, Thou art worthy to take the book, and to open the seals thereof: for thou wast slain, and hast redeemed us to Elohim (God) by thy blood out of every kindred, and tongue, and people, and nation;* (Revelation 5:9)

*Let the redeemed of Yahuah (LORD) say so, whom he hath redeemed from the hand of the enemy;* (Psalm 107:2)

*And gathered them out of the lands, from the east, and from the west, from the north, and from the south.* (Psalm 107:3)

*And Yahuah (LORD) shall scatter thee among all people, from the one end of the earth even unto the other; and there thou shalt serve other gods, which neither thou nor thy fathers have known, even wood and stone.* (Deuteronomy 28:64)

*And hast made us unto our Elohim (God) kings and priests: and we shall reign on the earth.* (Revelation 5:10)

The inherited reading hears the song of the Lamb as a body assembled from all humanity. The psalm it echoes has an older address: the redeemed of Yahuah (God), redeemed from the hand of the enemy, gathered out of the lands from all four directions. Why must the redeemed come out of every kindred, tongue, people, and nation? Because that is precisely where the covenant people was scattered — from the one end of the earth even unto the other. The redemption out of all nations answers the scattering into all nations, and the redeemed are made kings and priests to reign on the earth — the calling Yashar'el (Israel) carried from Sinai.$card$, '{"Psalm 107:2","Revelation 5:9"}'::TEXT[], 'free', NOW())
