INSERT INTO kingdom_verses (verse_id, strand, strand_label, card_title, card_md, anchor_refs, tier_required, last_reviewed_at)
VALUES ((SELECT v.id FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON c.id = v.chapter_id JOIN books b ON b.id = c.book_id JOIN editions e ON e.id = b.edition_id WHERE e.slug = 'canon' AND b.slug = 'zechariah' AND c.chapter_number = 11 AND v.verse_number = 14), 'gathering', 'The gathering', 'The staff called Bands — a brotherhood real enough to break', $card$*And I will feed the flock of slaughter, even you, O poor of the flock. And I took unto me two staves; the one I called Beauty, and the other I called Bands; and I fed the flock.* (Zechariah 11:7)

*Then I cut asunder mine other staff, even Bands, that I might break the brotherhood between Yahudah (Judah) and Yashar'el (Israel).* (Zechariah 11:14)

*And join them one to another into one stick; and they shall become one in thine hand.* (Ezekiel 37:17)

The shepherd carries two staves, and when he is rejected he cuts the one called Bands — *that I might break the brotherhood between Yahudah (Judah) and Yashar'el (Israel).* Scripture does not break what does not exist. The brotherhood of the two houses is real enough to be named, real enough to be severed — and Ezekiel holds the counterpart: two sticks joined one to another, one in his hand. A staff broken in one prophet and rejoined in another is not a metaphor about institutions. It is the two houses.$card$, '{"Zechariah 11:7","Zechariah 11:14","Ezekiel 37:17"}'::TEXT[], 'free', NOW())
