INSERT INTO kingdom_verses (verse_id, strand, strand_label, card_title, card_md, anchor_refs, tier_required, last_reviewed_at)
VALUES ((SELECT v.id FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON c.id = v.chapter_id JOIN books b ON b.id = c.book_id JOIN editions e ON e.id = b.edition_id WHERE e.slug = 'canon' AND b.slug = 'jeremiah' AND c.chapter_number = 31 AND v.verse_number = 27), 'gathering', 'The gathering', 'Sown together — the new covenant keeps both addressees', $card$*Behold, the days come, saith Yahuah (LORD), that I will sow the house of Yashar'el (Israel) and the house of Yahudah (Judah) with the seed of man, and with the seed of beast.* (Jeremiah 31:27)

*And it shall come to pass, that like as I have watched over them, to pluck up, and to break down, and to throw down, and to destroy, and to afflict; so will I watch over them, to build, and to plant, saith Yahuah (LORD).* (Jeremiah 31:28)

*For finding fault with them, he saith, Behold, the days come, saith Yahuah (Lord), when I will make a new covenant with the house of Yashar'el (Israel) and with the house of Yahudah (Judah):* (Hebrews 8:8)

Four verses before the new covenant is announced, its two addressees are sown side by side: the house of Yashar'el (Israel) and the house of Yahudah (Judah). And when the letter to the Hebrews quotes the covenant, it keeps the address line intact — both houses, named. A covenant made with two named bloodline houses cannot be re-addressed to an institution without calling the one who named them a liar. The same watching that plucked up now builds and plants — both.$card$, '{"Jeremiah 31:27-28","Hebrews 8:8"}'::TEXT[], 'free', NOW())
