INSERT INTO kingdom_verses (verse_id, strand, strand_label, card_title, card_md, anchor_refs, tier_required, last_reviewed_at)
VALUES ((SELECT v.id FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON c.id = v.chapter_id JOIN books b ON b.id = c.book_id JOIN editions e ON e.id = b.edition_id WHERE e.slug = 'canon' AND b.slug = 'matthew' AND c.chapter_number = 19 AND v.verse_number = 28), 'kingdom', 'The kingdom', 'Twelve thrones require twelve tribes', $card$*And Yahusha (Jesus) said unto them, Verily I say unto you, That ye which have followed me, in the regeneration when the Son of Adam shall sit in the throne of his glory, ye also shall sit upon twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Yashar'el (Israel).* (Matthew 19:28)

*All these are the twelve tribes of Yashar'el (Israel): and this is it that their father spake unto them, and blessed them; every one according to his blessing he blessed them.* (Genesis 49:28)

*Thus saith Adonai Yahuah (the Lord GOD); This shall be the border, whereby ye shall inherit the land according to the twelve tribes of Yashar'el (Israel): Joseph shall have two portions.* (Ezekiel 47:13)

*James, a servant of Elohim (God) and of the Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ), to the twelve tribes which are scattered abroad, greeting.* (James 1:1)

In the regeneration, twelve thrones judge *the twelve tribes of Yashar'el (Israel)* — the same twelve Jacob blessed, the same twelve Ezekiel's restored land is surveyed for, with Joseph given two portions so the arithmetic of the two houses still shows in the map. And James addresses his letter to those very tribes, *scattered abroad* — present tense, alive, findable by mail. The kingdom's government is not sized for an institution. It is sized for a family of twelve tribes in two houses, gathered and judged and planted, every throne matched to a tribe that still exists.$card$, '{"Genesis 49:28","Ezekiel 47:13","Matthew 19:28","James 1:1"}'::TEXT[], 'free', NOW())
