INSERT INTO kingdom_verses (verse_id, strand, strand_label, card_title, card_md, anchor_refs, tier_required, last_reviewed_at)
VALUES ((SELECT v.id FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON c.id = v.chapter_id JOIN books b ON b.id = c.book_id JOIN editions e ON e.id = b.edition_id WHERE e.slug = 'canon' AND b.slug = 'john' AND c.chapter_number = 4 AND v.verse_number = 22), 'teaching', 'The teaching', 'Ye worship ye know not what: the lost knowledge of the north country', $card$*And he must needs go through Samaria.* (John 4:4)

*Then cometh he to a city of Samaria, which is called Sychar, near to the parcel of ground that Jacob gave to his son Joseph.* (John 4:5)

*In the ninth year of Hoshea the king of Assyria took Samaria, and carried Yashar'el (Israel) away into Assyria, and placed them in Halah and in Habor by the river of Gozan, and in the cities of the Medes.* (2 Kings 17:6)

*Ye worship ye know not what: we know what we worship: for salvation is of the Yahudim (Jews).* (John 4:22)

*My people are destroyed for lack of knowledge: because thou hast rejected knowledge, I will also reject thee, that thou shalt be no priest to me: seeing thou hast forgotten the law of thy Elohim (God), I will also forget thy children.* (Hosea 4:6)

*But the hour cometh, and now is, when the true worshippers shall worship the Father in spirit and in truth: for the Father seeketh such to worship him.* (John 4:23)

He *must needs* go through Samaria — through the territory that was the northern kingdom's home ground before Assyria emptied it — and he sits down on the well Jacob dug, on the parcel Jacob gave to Joseph. The geography is the sermon. To the woman he names the condition that hangs over that ground: *ye worship ye know not what.* That is Hosea's verdict on the northern house in its own words — destroyed for lack of knowledge, the Torah of Elohim (God) forgotten. Worship without knowledge is what the scattering left behind on that soil. And into that condition he speaks the turning: the hour cometh, *and now is,* when true worshippers worship the Father in spirit and in truth — the knowledge coming back to the place that lost it.$card$, '{"Hosea 4:6","2 Kings 17:6","John 4:4-23"}'::TEXT[], 'free', NOW())
